00:02:48.584 --> 00:02:50.656
there are no mistakes
really, everything is a

00:02:50.656 --> 00:02:51.630
learning lesson.

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:52.984
- Everything helps you to do better.

00:02:52.984 --> 00:02:54.013
- Right.

00:02:54.013 --> 00:02:55.461
- So I talk about some of
the mistakes that I made,

00:02:55.461 --> 00:02:57.925
and it just helps you
to get further along,

00:02:57.925 --> 00:02:59.686
learn from those mistakes,

00:02:59.686 --> 00:03:00.904
and get smarter.

00:03:00.904 --> 00:03:02.990
My entrepreneurial spirit flourished

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:05.464
when I started thinking of ideas,

00:03:05.464 --> 00:03:07.131
and then seeing them
out there on the market.

00:03:07.131 --> 00:03:08.552
But I hadn't done that,

00:03:08.552 --> 00:03:09.531
someone else had.

00:03:09.531 --> 00:03:10.827
They were very successful.

00:03:10.827 --> 00:03:13.513
So when I thought of my
earring organizer, I thought,

00:03:13.513 --> 00:03:15.892
this time I'm going to do it, and I did.

00:03:15.892 --> 00:03:17.799
I knew that women had no good way,

00:03:17.799 --> 00:03:19.588
in which, to store their jewelry.

00:03:19.588 --> 00:03:20.914
And it just came to me,

00:03:20.914 --> 00:03:23.293
like a thunderbolt, and I
went home and I drew it,

00:03:23.293 --> 00:03:25.583
and then I went to my
grandfather's wood shop,

00:03:25.583 --> 00:03:26.707
and I made it.

00:03:26.707 --> 00:03:28.113
After I made my sample,

00:03:28.113 --> 00:03:30.795
I did market research to see
if people would really like it,

00:03:30.795 --> 00:03:31.851
or buy it.

00:03:31.851 --> 00:03:33.800
I started calling every
retailer in the country,

00:03:33.800 --> 00:03:36.303
let it ring a thousand
times until they'd pick up,

00:03:36.303 --> 00:03:40.514
and I flew myself to 21 cities in 18 days

00:03:40.514 --> 00:03:43.661
and met with different buyers
and showed them my prototype.

00:03:43.661 --> 00:03:46.107
That first product was very successful.

00:03:46.107 --> 00:03:48.570
I made well over a million dollars on it.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.506
And, I started thinking,

00:03:50.506 --> 00:03:52.577
wow there's lot's of other
things that I could make.

00:03:52.577 --> 00:03:54.675
And I started making cosmetic organizers,

00:03:54.675 --> 00:03:56.815
I started doing kitchen gadgets.

00:03:56.815 --> 00:03:59.116
My goal was to improve people's lives

00:03:59.116 --> 00:04:00.755
with the products that I created.

00:04:00.755 --> 00:04:03.813
To date, I've created over 400 products,

00:04:03.813 --> 00:04:06.806
and I've generated half
a billion in sales.

00:04:06.806 --> 00:04:07.793
To me,

00:04:07.793 --> 00:04:10.799
an entrepreneur is somebody
who will do whatever it takes.

00:04:10.799 --> 00:04:11.632
- [Interviewer] Right.

00:04:11.632 --> 00:04:15.525
- They're driven, they
are A-type personalities.

00:04:15.525 --> 00:04:16.358
They,

00:04:17.786 --> 00:04:19.517
it's like they don't know the word no.

00:04:19.517 --> 00:04:21.012
And that's always been my mantra.

00:04:21.012 --> 00:04:22.620
I know no noes, just, how can I?

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:23.453
So,

00:04:24.323 --> 00:04:27.902
when I see that person I
know that no matter what,

00:04:27.902 --> 00:04:29.671
even if they have to pivot, you know,

00:04:29.671 --> 00:04:30.728
which is something that happens.

00:04:30.728 --> 00:04:32.012
Maybe this isn't the best idea,

00:04:32.012 --> 00:04:34.235
but something else is and
you're going to change it,

00:04:34.235 --> 00:04:35.709
they're still going to make it,

00:04:35.709 --> 00:04:37.728
because they have what it takes

00:04:37.728 --> 00:04:40.111
to be a successful entrepreneur.

00:04:40.111 --> 00:04:42.463
- [Kudlow] New business
formations are way down.

00:04:42.463 --> 00:04:43.296
- Way down.

00:04:43.296 --> 00:04:45.350
- [Kudlow] Way down, and
venture capital is way down.

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:46.183
- Well ...

00:04:46.183 --> 00:04:47.896
- That means people are
afraid of something.

00:04:47.896 --> 00:04:50.686
These are brand new business start-ups,

00:04:50.686 --> 00:04:52.351
a very important economic measure.

00:04:52.351 --> 00:04:53.311
Way down.

00:04:53.311 --> 00:04:55.072
- Well I think, to me,

00:04:55.072 --> 00:04:56.386
I'm an entrepreneur,

00:04:56.386 --> 00:04:58.631
and I think that true entrepreneurs,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.893
it doesn't really matter
what's going on in the economy.

00:05:01.893 --> 00:05:04.792
If they come up with a great
business idea, great product,

00:05:04.792 --> 00:05:07.539
they're risk takers,
they're going to go for it.

00:05:07.539 --> 00:05:09.125
It doesn't matter if the taxes are up 5%,

00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:12.589
it doesn't matter what
is going on with that,

00:05:12.589 --> 00:05:15.014
they are people that just are pioneers,

00:05:15.014 --> 00:05:16.433
they're going to forge ahead,

00:05:16.433 --> 00:05:19.058
and start that business no matter what.

00:05:19.058 --> 00:05:21.402
Well, I've launched, in the last 16 years,

00:05:21.402 --> 00:05:22.819
400 new products.

00:05:23.905 --> 00:05:25.934
And I have a 115 patents.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:27.804
- People going through this
now have a lot of options.

00:05:27.804 --> 00:05:29.999
You have fund-raising
cites like Kickstarter,

00:05:29.999 --> 00:05:32.326
you have little online
market places like Etsy.

00:05:32.326 --> 00:05:34.384
Do you recommend that people use these

00:05:34.384 --> 00:05:35.966
to sort of test out their products?

00:05:35.966 --> 00:05:37.633
- I think a lot of people

00:05:37.633 --> 00:05:39.718
don't trust their gut enough.

00:05:39.718 --> 00:05:41.289
I think a lot of people want somebody

00:05:41.289 --> 00:05:43.401
to hold their hand through the process.

00:05:43.401 --> 00:05:45.482
And really, that's not the best way.

00:05:45.482 --> 00:05:47.446
There's no special formula that's right

00:05:47.446 --> 00:05:48.856
for every single person.

00:05:48.856 --> 00:05:51.239
You have to decide, do
you like Kickstarter,

00:05:51.239 --> 00:05:52.860
do you feel that's right for you.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:55.489
Or, you know, people have other
ways in which to do things.

00:05:55.489 --> 00:05:58.360
So I think it's know your options.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.767
- It's got to feel good when
someone brings you a new idea.

00:06:00.767 --> 00:06:01.876
- Well I love it.

00:06:01.876 --> 00:06:03.268
I mean, that's what drives me.

00:06:03.268 --> 00:06:05.696
- I love the excitement
of taking a product

00:06:05.696 --> 00:06:07.984
and turning it into a huge success.

00:06:07.984 --> 00:06:10.515
So, you know, that's what
Shark Tank's all about,

00:06:10.515 --> 00:06:11.894
and that's what my book is all about.

00:06:11.894 --> 00:06:12.922
It's exciting!

00:06:12.922 --> 00:06:14.047
- What are some of the key traits

00:06:14.047 --> 00:06:15.537
to being a successful inventor?

00:06:15.537 --> 00:06:18.337
- Well, I think definitely,
you have to be driven,

00:06:18.337 --> 00:06:20.599
you have to be motivated,
you have to have passion,

00:06:20.599 --> 00:06:23.619
you have to be somebody, who,
like I said there are no noes.

00:06:23.619 --> 00:06:25.695
You know, if I have an obstacle,

00:06:25.695 --> 00:06:28.574
I go over it, I go under
it, I go around it.

00:06:28.574 --> 00:06:29.407
- Right.

00:06:29.407 --> 00:06:30.794
- You just don't quit.

00:06:30.794 --> 00:06:31.657
- I go through it!

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:32.675
- I go through it!

00:06:32.675 --> 00:06:34.786
(audience claps)

00:06:34.786 --> 00:06:37.953
- Well, I think that start-ups should,

00:06:37.953 --> 00:06:40.659
one, be willing to do
everything that it takes

00:06:40.659 --> 00:06:42.485
to make their start-up work.

00:06:42.485 --> 00:06:44.841
You know, a lot of people
say, "Oh, well, you know,

00:06:44.841 --> 00:06:46.723
"I just want to do it
for a few hours a day."

00:06:46.723 --> 00:06:47.766
(chuckling)

00:06:47.766 --> 00:06:49.056
That's not going to happen.

00:06:49.056 --> 00:06:50.759
If you want to start your own business,

00:06:50.759 --> 00:06:52.710
you really need to put in
the time and dedication

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:56.092
and that means 24/7, if need be.

00:06:56.092 --> 00:06:59.478
Make sure whatever your idea
is that people really want it,

00:06:59.478 --> 00:07:00.562
and need it.

00:07:00.562 --> 00:07:03.212
And the way to learn that is
to do some market research.

00:07:03.212 --> 00:07:05.582
Don't just ask friends and family.

00:07:05.582 --> 00:07:07.654
Get out there and ask a lot of people,

00:07:07.654 --> 00:07:08.928
and a variety of people.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:10.338
If they like your idea,

00:07:10.338 --> 00:07:11.742
and if they would buy it,

00:07:11.742 --> 00:07:13.488
use it, or pay for it.

00:07:13.488 --> 00:07:16.061
And if so, what would
they be willing to pay.

00:07:16.061 --> 00:07:18.793
Make sure that you've
done all of your research,

00:07:18.793 --> 00:07:21.627
and what it takes to get
your product idea out there.

00:07:21.627 --> 00:07:23.115
So, have a business plan,

00:07:23.115 --> 00:07:26.039
and find out all the steps required first,

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:28.324
so that you're not missing
anything along the way,

00:07:28.324 --> 00:07:29.776
and you don't mess anything up.

00:07:29.776 --> 00:07:31.302
Make sure that you learn

00:07:31.302 --> 00:07:33.512
all the people that you
can market your product to.

00:07:33.512 --> 00:07:36.921
Stores, shopping channels, whatever it is,

00:07:36.921 --> 00:07:38.261
make sure that you know them,

00:07:38.261 --> 00:07:39.631
and that you're aggressive,

00:07:39.631 --> 00:07:42.160
and you're very
enthusiastic and passionate

00:07:42.160 --> 00:07:43.878
about your product idea or business

00:07:43.878 --> 00:07:46.343
because your enthusiasm
becomes infectious.

00:07:46.343 --> 00:07:48.617
If you believe in yourself, they will too.

00:07:48.617 --> 00:07:50.728
If you really have a drive,

00:07:50.728 --> 00:07:52.611
and really put your heart
and soul into something,

00:07:52.611 --> 00:07:54.911
you can really make anything happen.

00:07:54.911 --> 00:07:56.306
I'm a true believer in that.

00:07:56.306 --> 00:07:57.457
So,

00:07:57.457 --> 00:07:58.663
I think that we,

00:07:58.663 --> 00:08:01.521
hopefully, we make people
believe that they can achieve

00:08:01.521 --> 00:08:03.088
the American dream too.

00:08:03.088 --> 00:08:04.591
Just watch, study us, and

00:08:04.591 --> 00:08:07.703
if you really are passionate
and driven you can get there.

00:08:07.703 --> 00:08:09.703
My true feeling is this.

00:08:10.696 --> 00:08:12.335
No matter who you are,

00:08:12.335 --> 00:08:15.057
no matter what age you are,

00:08:15.057 --> 00:08:17.790
no matter the time in your life,

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.480
if you have a dream,

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:21.360
and you have the drive,

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:23.777
you can make anything happen.

00:08:24.694 --> 00:08:27.129
And if you are ever feeling down,

00:08:27.129 --> 00:08:29.460
or feeling like you
can't get over that hump,

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:31.863
